WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:04.817
One of the problems I run into when
talking to people about symbolism

00:00:04.857 --> 00:00:09.297
is the whole problem of the "literal versus
metaphor idea" - and I've talked about this

00:00:09.381 --> 00:00:15.062
a little bit before -; I want
to dive into that problem and show you

00:00:15.087 --> 00:00:19.894
that, in fact, it isn't very
much of a problem once you realize that

00:00:20.007 --> 00:00:22.728
there is no such thing as literal.

00:00:35.563 --> 00:00:39.463
(Opening) This is Jonathan Pageau,
welcome to "The Symbolic World".

00:00:47.788 --> 00:00:50.362
I already hear a bunch of
people screaming:

00:00:50.408 --> 00:00:53.289
"No! He's saying that
the Bible didn't happen!";

00:00:53.379 --> 00:00:56.021
"He is saying that everything
is just a metaphor!";

00:00:56.098 --> 00:01:00.410
not exactly: I'm trying to break that
duality - I'm really trying to destroy it -

00:01:00.464 --> 00:01:04.931
because it is really not useful in
understanding how meaning occurs and

00:01:05.011 --> 00:01:07.522
how things manifest themselves.

00:01:07.596 --> 00:01:11.671
When I say that "there's no such thing as
literal", what I mean by "literal" is this

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:17.716
strange pervasive idea - that is still
there in the West, it seems - that there is

00:01:17.773 --> 00:01:23.979
such a thing as a "direct description of
something", that there is such a thing as

00:01:24.104 --> 00:01:30.364
a description of something which is not
bound up in meaning and which is not

00:01:30.568 --> 00:01:36.534
bound up in narrative, or in an image; that
it is somehow a "meaningless description"...

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.930
...which is not already imbibed in meaning.

00:01:43.858 --> 00:01:47.202
You get that all the time,
when you talk to people...

00:01:49.017 --> 00:01:52.959
...In terms of a story,
in terms of the Bible, especially,

00:01:53.021 --> 00:01:58.165
people will argue over whether or not
the description in the Bible are "literal".

00:01:59.625 --> 00:02:03.434
To be honest with you, at this
point in my life, at this point in my

00:02:03.457 --> 00:02:09.040
understanding, I don't see what that
even means; I can understand - in the

00:02:09.109 --> 00:02:13.679
way that people talk about it - what it is
that they seem to be inferring: that it is

00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:19.798
somehow a "neutral description" of reality
that doesn't already have value,

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:24.176
or meaning in it, but I don't
understand how that is possible;

00:02:24.272 --> 00:02:28.475
because when you describe something, no
matter what it is that you describe, you have

00:02:28.626 --> 00:02:33.932
to have a purpose to describe it:
you need a "frame" in order to talk

00:02:33.972 --> 00:02:36.220
about something;

00:02:36.312 --> 00:02:42.231
like I've told you a million times before,
reality is too big - there are too many

00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:47.958
details in it -, and if I describe a series
of events, I will do it with a purpose,

00:02:48.091 --> 00:02:50.934
to make you understand something;

00:02:51.482 --> 00:02:56.532
I have to focus my attention on something,
because around the event that I'm describing

00:02:56.566 --> 00:03:01.484
there are a million other events going on
that I'm not describing, and the question is:

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:05.540
"why am I describing these events
and not describing these other events"?

00:03:05.805 --> 00:03:13.760
Already, that harms the problem of this
notion of literal - because if...

00:03:18.338 --> 00:03:21.607
...if I am telling a story about something,
and I'm not talking about

00:03:21.669 --> 00:03:28.000
the folds in their shirt, or about
the fact that they cut themselves shaving

00:03:28.054 --> 00:03:31.993
in the morning, I'm not talking about
those things because they're not relevant to

00:03:32.061 --> 00:03:34.578
what it is that I'm trying to get to;

00:03:34.635 --> 00:03:40.290
they're not part of the purpose
for which I'm describing something.

00:03:41.006 --> 00:03:44.596
Depending on the purpose for which
I'm describing something, I will use

00:03:44.709 --> 00:03:51.544
different types of language to describe it -
and the idea that somehow "accuracy",

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:58.405
in this kind of "scientific sense",
is somehow always desirable

00:03:58.455 --> 00:04:02.050
is of course completely wrong;
it is completely absurd

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:08.998
because accuracy can also fall
into an indefinite amount of detail.

00:04:10.152 --> 00:04:16.377
Let's say that I am describing a fight
and I want you to understand what happened.

00:04:17.889 --> 00:04:22.951
I could use a language that is extremely
accurate and say something like:

00:04:24.687 --> 00:04:28.855
"The guy put his left foot in front
of his front foot; and then the other

00:04:28.902 --> 00:04:34.518
"person's right hand came at this speed
towards his face, and he slightly flinched

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:40.374
"when the fist hit his face: he displaced
so many hairs and displaced so many pores -

00:04:42.657 --> 00:04:47.761
"so many tissues in his cheek
were disturbed;

00:04:49.648 --> 00:04:53.217
"and then his head moved three
centimeters to the left, and then it

00:04:53.251 --> 00:04:55.594
moved forward four centimeters backwards".

00:04:55.661 --> 00:05:00.488
I can go on and on, and I could describe
extremely accurately the event, but,

00:05:00.568 --> 00:05:05.308
as I'm describing it accurately,
I'm not getting to the purpose that

00:05:05.387 --> 00:05:09.757
I'm describing the event for,
that I'm describing this event to you for.

00:05:10.162 --> 00:05:13.609
I could say something like:
"the guy got smashed";

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.166
"he got his ass kicked";

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:22.334
I could use all this hyperbolic language in
order to help you understand what happened

00:05:22.549 --> 00:05:27.482
in the fight, and in the end my hyperbolic
language - the fact that I'll use...

00:05:28.855 --> 00:05:32.541
...exaggerations, that I'll use figures of
speech, that I'll use all these different...

00:05:34.355 --> 00:05:39.526
...ways of talking about reality - will end
up being truer to the purpose, that I'm

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:43.567
using to describe the event, than if I
was accurate in describing it.

00:05:43.774 --> 00:05:48.309
That's extremely important to understand,
especially if we're looking at stories

00:05:48.366 --> 00:05:50.366
in the Bible; ...

00:05:53.107 --> 00:05:56.585
...each book in the Bible has
different ways of describing things

00:05:56.710 --> 00:06:01.828
which are based on the purpose that they
are being described for - and so there are

00:06:01.918 --> 00:06:05.919
different styles, different ways, there
are different analogies which can be

00:06:05.977 --> 00:06:12.296
used in order to help you understand the
reason for which a text is being described.

00:06:12.791 --> 00:06:18.888
Therefore, this idea that you can somehow
get to this "literal description

00:06:18.956 --> 00:06:26.396
of reality" is extremely problematic and
it's not useful: it's better to rather

00:06:26.431 --> 00:06:30.906
understand the purpose
for which a story is being told.

00:06:30.997 --> 00:06:37.049
Even a scientific theory is never
literal -  in the sense of a neutral

00:06:37.185 --> 00:06:41.298
description of reality -:
when you do a scientific experiment,

00:06:41.344 --> 00:06:46.892
you have to frame that scientific experiment
extremely narrowly, because, like I said,

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:52.351
there are too many details; if
my purpose in a scientific experiment is

00:06:52.419 --> 00:06:57.654
to prove something about water, I will
not give you descriptions of trees or

00:06:57.722 --> 00:07:03.280
descriptions of rocks: I will talk
about the fact, the thing that I'm trying

00:07:03.383 --> 00:07:10.046
to describe; and as a result, that frame will
be extremely narrow and I will use a

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:15.656
certain type of language, quantifiable
language, in order to describe the

00:07:15.736 --> 00:07:18.205
phenomena that I'm explaining to you.

00:07:18.546 --> 00:07:22.231
The purpose is that you can
understand the mechanistic causes

00:07:22.344 --> 00:07:26.865
that bring it about - and, knowing that,
maybe reproduce it mechanistically -;

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:31.024
but, when we're telling or when we're
describing an event, that's not always

00:07:31.114 --> 00:07:36.453
the reason why we're describing it;
like I said: using figures of speech can

00:07:36.623 --> 00:07:43.543
sometimes be more effective
and more powerful than using just

00:07:43.676 --> 00:07:45.921
this kind of quantifiable language.

00:07:46.083 --> 00:07:49.666
If I use figures of speech
or if I use analogies to describe

00:07:49.713 --> 00:07:52.714
something, does it mean that I'm not
describing an event? Of course not!

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:57.209
Of course I can still be describing
an event, despite the fact that I'm using

00:07:57.311 --> 00:08:00.343
different types of ways of explaining it.

00:08:00.915 --> 00:08:06.524
The stretch that I'm asking you to make
is very important: the Christian way of

00:08:06.615 --> 00:08:08.720
describing reality is that

00:08:08.747 --> 00:08:13.366
the world is made by "Logos" - the world
is made by meaning and purpose -;

00:08:16.205 --> 00:08:22.268
the very cosmology in which Christianity
exists excludes the idea that there could

00:08:22.325 --> 00:08:27.621
be some kind of "neutral reality" that
exists at the bottom somehow,

00:08:27.700 --> 00:08:34.297
and that is not informed with meaning
by Logos - the Bible itself describes the

00:08:34.354 --> 00:08:39.672
creation process as a process which is full
of meaning and purpose -;

00:08:41.273 --> 00:08:45.577
therefore, I don't understand how,
despite that, people can somehow still

00:08:45.634 --> 00:08:48.771
have this weird idea of this neutral
reality which exists underneath.

00:08:50.881 --> 00:08:54.828
The world of Christianity is a
meeting of Heaven and Earth, it's

00:08:54.901 --> 00:09:02.475
a meeting of patterns, Logos, meaning,
purpose and this "potentiality" which

00:09:02.588 --> 00:09:06.270
is there at the bottom - maybe
you don't like the word

00:09:06.338 --> 00:09:08.548
"potentiality", you can use another word -:

00:09:08.581 --> 00:09:11.131
St. Maximus talks about Logos and "Tropos" -

00:09:11.186 --> 00:09:15.997
that is this notion of purpose and
meaning, and then the particularities of

00:09:16.077 --> 00:09:22.567
something -, and those two have to join
together, and you could call it a

00:09:22.613 --> 00:09:27.723
"mini-incarnation" - it's not an incarnation
in the same way that Christ is incarnated,

00:09:27.791 --> 00:09:32.430
but it is analogous to the Incarnation,
in the sense that it's an invisible meaning

00:09:32.475 --> 00:09:36.191
and purpose which join a kind of
"indefinite particularity"-;

00:09:36.259 --> 00:09:40.481
and that meaning together is
where reality exists:

00:09:40.614 --> 00:09:44.273
that's where the world, where life
where all of these things are -

00:09:44.965 --> 00:09:49.543
and once that starts to break
in our thinking, a lot of things become

00:09:49.623 --> 00:09:55.330
less problematic, a lot of things become
less difficult to deal with.

00:09:57.354 --> 00:10:02.558
One of the problems that we have is that
people seem to want - let's say

00:10:02.626 --> 00:10:06.478
they're reading the story in Genesis,
they're reading the description of

00:10:06.546 --> 00:10:12.628
Creation - they want to get to this event:
they somehow think that they can access

00:10:12.962 --> 00:10:18.624
this neutral event which is behind the
story - you don't have access to that,

00:10:19.914 --> 00:10:25.134
you can't get to it because it doesn't
exist, it doesn't exist on its own -;

00:10:25.928 --> 00:10:31.017
the events that happen, as far
as they are described, are this "framing",

00:10:31.173 --> 00:10:34.234
this coming together of meaning
and particulars.

00:10:35.196 --> 00:10:39.141
What we have is the story.
Especially when we're talking

00:10:39.187 --> 00:10:45.045
about something like the Creation story
or the ancient stories that have been

00:10:45.102 --> 00:10:48.833
around for thousands of years, what we have
is the story:

00:10:49.809 --> 00:10:55.841
to try to somehow get to what
is behind the story in this neutral manner

00:10:55.948 --> 00:10:58.261
is not the right way to go;

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:02.593
people do think that, somehow, they can
try - through these archaeological

00:11:02.695 --> 00:11:05.961
methods or through these historical
methods - to get to what is

00:11:06.032 --> 00:11:10.811
behind the story in Genesis,
but it's a futile trip;

00:11:10.913 --> 00:11:16.398
and it's especially futile if you think that,
once you get there, that what you're going to

00:11:16.489 --> 00:11:21.150
get ... - from using archaeological methods
or using these different new scientific

00:11:21.241 --> 00:11:27.921
ways of breaking down the text into all
these different sources, or

00:11:28.008 --> 00:11:31.714
whatever people come up with in the modern
world - ... you're not going to get to

00:11:31.778 --> 00:11:37.169
something which is truer than
what the story is offering you;

00:11:37.262 --> 00:11:42.168
and once you understand that, then
a lot of things are going to free

00:11:42.225 --> 00:11:45.208
up in your mind, and a lot of problems
are going to go away.

00:11:46.167 --> 00:11:50.771
One of the examples that
I like to use is the

00:11:50.915 --> 00:11:55.485
example of the prophecy that Elijah is

00:11:55.547 --> 00:11:58.906
going to come before the Messiah -
there's this prophecy, which is in the Old

00:11:58.941 --> 00:12:03.496
Testament, which said that Elijah is
going to come back, that he is going to

00:12:03.553 --> 00:12:05.553
show himself before the Messiah.

00:12:05.689 --> 00:12:10.860
Therefore, when Christ is there and His
disciples ask Him about this prophecy, ...

00:12:12.645 --> 00:12:20.431
...and Christ tells them that "Saint John
the Baptist is the Elijah that was to come

00:12:20.579 --> 00:12:24.162
before the Messiah", and He says "if you're
able to receive this,

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:26.876
that is what happened", ...

00:12:29.535 --> 00:12:36.674
...if the question is posed: "did Elijah
come before the Messiah?", the answer is

00:12:36.861 --> 00:12:42.628
"yes, Elijah did come before the Messiah,
and that Elijah was St. John the Baptist".

00:12:43.404 --> 00:12:50.007
Do you see what I'm doing there?
I'm not trying to get to this weird

00:12:50.087 --> 00:12:55.727
"literal-neutral reality" behind it:
I'm trying to show you how Christ can

00:12:55.818 --> 00:13:02.932
quite easily take this prophecy and show that
it's actually a pattern of reality which

00:13:03.012 --> 00:13:07.197
is manifesting itself - and here is the
manner in which it manifested itself, with

00:13:07.322 --> 00:13:12.095
Elijah as this pattern, and St. John the
Baptist, with those two coming together;

00:13:12.186 --> 00:13:19.194
and so the answer to "did Elijah manifest
himself before the Messiah" is "yes".

00:13:21.086 --> 00:13:25.675
That is the answer that I will give
to everything:

00:13:27.361 --> 00:13:30.188
-"Did Adam and Eve fall in the garden?"
-"Yes";

00:13:30.392 --> 00:13:33.182
-"Did Adam and Eve eat the apple
in the garden?" -"Yes";

00:13:34.388 --> 00:13:39.396
I have no problem saying that all of these
things are true and that they are the best

00:13:39.465 --> 00:13:42.912
description of that event, and the best
description of that reality;

00:13:42.989 --> 00:13:47.921
I'm not trying to get, in some
weird scientific sense, behind the story

00:13:48.001 --> 00:13:51.758
to find out what it is that "really
happened" - I don't know what you're

00:13:51.816 --> 00:13:55.655
talking about when you say this,
I have no idea what it is that you

00:13:55.781 --> 00:13:57.781
think you're going to get to -;

00:13:57.841 --> 00:14:00.649
that story is the story that was
given to us as the description

00:14:00.718 --> 00:14:05.854
of this extremely important event, and
the question of how to describe that story:

00:14:06.486 --> 00:14:10.564
that's it, that's the story, that's the
story we have, and that's the best way to

00:14:10.683 --> 00:14:12.976
describe that event.

00:14:13.892 --> 00:14:18.372
As I have already said, a lot of the
problems and a lot of the difficulties that

00:14:18.451 --> 00:14:21.361
modern Christians have come from the fact
that, without even knowing it,

00:14:21.486 --> 00:14:26.286
they have completely taken upon themselves
the kind of "modern scientific

00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:30.467
view of the world"
as being the highest reality.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:36.674
When I was younger, I remember hearing
a Protestant tell me that "science is just

00:14:36.799 --> 00:14:41.305
the mind of God" - well, it's a serious
problem to engage the world that way, ...

00:14:42.999 --> 00:14:48.055
...because, then, you always end up trying
to get behind the story and to find

00:14:48.138 --> 00:14:51.120
some scientific description there -:

00:14:51.529 --> 00:14:53.558
well, that description is not there

00:14:53.650 --> 00:14:56.634
because science is not the first
degree of reality;

00:14:56.792 --> 00:15:00.014
science is great, it's fine, as
I've always told you, to

00:15:00.086 --> 00:15:03.910
fly airplanes and to make medicine - for
that purpose, it is wonderful, and it works,

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:06.688
and it does what it's supposed to do -,

00:15:09.473 --> 00:15:12.260
but that is not the only way
to describe reality,

00:15:12.293 --> 00:15:16.537
and it is not the best way to describe
reality, if your purpose is to show people

00:15:16.562 --> 00:15:20.865
how to live; if your purpose is to help
people understand events that happened

00:15:20.937 --> 00:15:22.937
so long ago...

00:15:25.478 --> 00:15:28.937
...that you won't even
be able to connect to the reference

00:15:28.986 --> 00:15:34.906
points in the scientific way, then we use
story tropes - manners of describing

00:15:34.961 --> 00:15:37.431
that are the best way to
describe that event.

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:44.185
Consequently, it is
extremely problematic to say that...

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:51.919
...there is this weird opposition
between literal and metaphorical.

00:15:54.497 --> 00:15:58.297
There are other people
who somehow think that the metaphor is

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:01.763
going to save them as well, that,
somehow, saying that "something is a

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:04.303
metaphor" is going to get them
out of trouble.

00:16:04.591 --> 00:16:08.352
This is particularly true of
Communion.

00:16:09.089 --> 00:16:11.735
I've seen this happen so many times

00:16:11.793 --> 00:16:15.240
in YouTube comments, people bringing
this up when I talk about Communion,

00:16:15.297 --> 00:16:18.411
and I talk about the reality of Communion
and the fact that...

00:16:20.441 --> 00:16:23.616
...this is truly
the Body and Blood of Christ -

00:16:24.625 --> 00:16:27.767
obviously someone
will show up and say: "No, it's not.

00:16:27.847 --> 00:16:30.953
"It's so disturbing to say that because
this is a weird cannibalistic thing.

00:16:31.022 --> 00:16:35.940
"It's just a symbol, it's just
a metaphor; Christ is saying that this

00:16:36.121 --> 00:16:39.444
is a metaphor for His Body and Blood"; ...

00:16:40.945 --> 00:16:43.082
...and because of that, somehow, they think

00:16:43.138 --> 00:16:44.974
they're getting out of the problem.

00:16:45.043 --> 00:16:48.267
Well, you're not getting out of the problem.
First of all, I will not accord to you

00:16:48.358 --> 00:16:51.545
when you say that "it is just
a metaphor", ...

00:16:53.016 --> 00:16:55.458
...but let's say that I did -

00:16:55.533 --> 00:16:58.754
let's say that I gave that to you, let's say
that I gave the fact that

00:16:58.810 --> 00:17:00.822
"it's just a metaphor" to you -:

00:17:00.913 --> 00:17:03.260
how are you getting out
of the problem?

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:06.548
You're saying that this idea
is very disturbing,

00:17:06.614 --> 00:17:09.237
that we would eat the
Real Body and Blood of Christ;

00:17:09.313 --> 00:17:11.814
but do you not think that
it would be disturbing to

00:17:11.868 --> 00:17:14.196
eat the "metaphorical body and
blood" of Christ as well?

00:17:14.241 --> 00:17:19.242
Why is that not as weird and as
disturbing as saying that it's real?

00:17:21.043 --> 00:17:25.333
I'm gonna be a bit disturbing
right now, but let's say that some

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:31.230
weird cult came up with a ritual where
they eat the feces of someone, ...

00:17:34.047 --> 00:17:38.537
...or where they have a kind of "inverse
satanic communion" where they

00:17:38.605 --> 00:17:42.578
eat the feces of their
master or whatever else;

00:17:42.908 --> 00:17:45.498
and then someone from this cult could say:

00:17:45.584 --> 00:17:49.538
"Oh, no. We're not 'really' eating
the feces of our master,

00:17:49.618 --> 00:17:54.153
"it's just a 'metaphorical eating'
of the feces - we just make this bread

00:17:54.233 --> 00:17:56.947
in the form of feces and then we eat it".

00:17:59.094 --> 00:18:01.929
Why would that be less weird?
Why is that less disturbing?

00:18:01.986 --> 00:18:03.986
Why is that less of a problem?

00:18:04.038 --> 00:18:09.159
It's the best for you to deal with the
the mystery -

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.250
you can't totally deal with it -,

00:18:11.336 --> 00:18:15.426
but it's best to face the mystery
of Communion rather than try to skirt

00:18:15.494 --> 00:18:20.767
around it; it's better than to avoid it
by saying that, somehow, because you think

00:18:20.858 --> 00:18:24.805
that something is "just a metaphor",
that it is meaningless: it's not!

00:18:26.597 --> 00:18:30.317
I keep joking around with this idea -
my brother and I, we always say that

00:18:30.396 --> 00:18:33.863
"there's no such thing as literal and
there is no metaphor" -;

00:18:34.011 --> 00:18:37.661
that's not how things work,
it's not that simple -

00:18:37.719 --> 00:18:40.796
you can't just throw
something away and say:

00:18:40.842 --> 00:18:42.757
"That's just a metaphor" -;

00:18:42.803 --> 00:18:45.195
well, there's a reason
why you're using that metaphor -

00:18:45.226 --> 00:18:48.190
even if it's "just a metaphor" -,
there's a reason why you're...

00:18:50.772 --> 00:18:56.108
...using those words and that
purpose, even if it's "just literal" -

00:18:56.431 --> 00:18:59.458
these terms are not useful
to help us understand how

00:18:59.504 --> 00:19:02.543
meaning occurs and how things unfold.

00:19:02.805 --> 00:19:09.268
In terms of Communion, to understand
this problem of the Body and Blood,

00:19:09.349 --> 00:19:12.515
not to understand it,
but to deal with this problem -

00:19:12.561 --> 00:19:15.861
and to deal with
the idea that it's neither

00:19:15.952 --> 00:19:20.601
literal, in the scientific sense,
nor is it a metaphor, in the...

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:27.640
...modern way of understanding a metaphor,
that it is something that is symbolic,

00:19:27.709 --> 00:19:30.397
in the way that I'm trying to explain -

00:19:30.545 --> 00:19:35.453
this is something which is, by the
bringing together of elements,

00:19:35.579 --> 00:19:41.581
and just joining with a spiritual essence,
the way that reality functions.

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:49.226
You could get to the same idea, to the same
understanding, for example, when we say that

00:19:49.407 --> 00:19:52.877
"The Church is the Body of Christ":

00:19:53.021 --> 00:19:56.536
is that "literal" or is
that a "metaphor"?

00:19:56.627 --> 00:20:00.630
It's neither of those: it's
not literal and it's not a metaphor,

00:20:00.733 --> 00:20:05.200
it's a symbolic truth - it's
a symbolic truth which can help you

00:20:05.304 --> 00:20:11.574
understand what a body is, and
how a body comes together and manifests

00:20:11.643 --> 00:20:14.992
something which is above it, how it
manifests something spiritual; ...

00:20:16.205 --> 00:20:20.594
...anything that is a body
is always an accumulation of parts,

00:20:20.697 --> 00:20:27.152
and just because you visually see those
parts close together in your perception,

00:20:27.414 --> 00:20:31.881
does it mean that they aren't parts
which are also separate from each other?

00:20:33.451 --> 00:20:38.616
In your body, there's a lot of space between
your molecules, and if you think that

00:20:38.695 --> 00:20:42.940
that relative amount of space between
your molecules is not bothersome,

00:20:42.986 --> 00:20:47.083
but the bigger amount of space
between the members of The Church

00:20:47.197 --> 00:20:51.090
is a problem - so now that can't
be a body -, that's a wrong thought!

00:20:51.147 --> 00:20:56.156
Yes, that can be a body: an accumulation
of people can also be a body, just like the

00:20:56.236 --> 00:21:01.418
accumulation of your molecules can also
be a body - and the way that that happens

00:21:01.588 --> 00:21:05.720
is neither literal nor is it a metaphor.

00:21:05.902 --> 00:21:08.495
It is symbolic, ...

00:21:10.297 --> 00:21:14.670
...it is the unity of multiplicity which
appears to us and which shows us

00:21:14.796 --> 00:21:19.196
the spiritual essence, the Logos,
the purpose which makes us

00:21:19.276 --> 00:21:22.935
engage with something as one, as a unity.

00:21:23.389 --> 00:21:27.959
I hope that that's a little
bit helpful in understanding why,

00:21:28.666 --> 00:21:34.460
if you engage with me with
those types of languages of

00:21:34.563 --> 00:21:39.893
literal and metaphorical, why all
of that is not useful to help you

00:21:39.995 --> 00:21:42.150
understand the world.

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:46.183
I hope this has helped,
and I will get to talk with

00:21:46.286 --> 00:21:48.447
you again very soon.

00:21:49.325 --> 00:21:52.205
If you enjoy The Symbolic World content,
there's a lot of things you can do

00:21:52.307 --> 00:21:54.862
to help us out: if you are
not subscribed, please do;

00:21:54.897 --> 00:21:57.539
go ahead and share this to
all your friends,

00:21:57.709 --> 00:21:59.754
if you can get involved in the discussion;

00:21:59.839 --> 00:22:04.015
we have a Facebook group in which people
can talk about these subjects - I will put

00:22:04.061 --> 00:22:07.776
all those links in the description -; and
also, if you can, please support us

00:22:07.878 --> 00:22:13.355
financially by going to my website
www.thesymbolicworld.com/support  ;

00:22:13.541 --> 00:22:16.860
I also have a Patreon and a SubscribeStar.

00:22:16.902 --> 00:22:19.162
Thanks again, I'll see you soon.

